---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';

const description =
  'ScrubKit is a privacy-first browser toolkit for cleaning messy text and data — free, signup-free, and built to run entirely on your device.';
---

<Base title="About ScrubKit — Privacy-First Text Tools" description={description}>
  <div class="container-page pt-8">
    <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />

    <header class="mt-6 max-w-3xl">
      <span class="eyebrow text-ink-3">About</span>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold sm:text-5xl">
        Small tools, honest engineering.
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-page mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Why ScrubKit exists</h2>
      <p>
        Cleaning a list should not require an account. Searching for “remove
        duplicate lines” today lands you on pages stuffed with ads, fake
        download buttons and upload forms that quietly send your data through
        someone else's server — for a job your browser can do instantly on its
        own.
      </p>
      <p>
        ScrubKit takes the opposite position: every tool is a real, working
        page first, and the site around it stays out of the way. No signup, no
        usage caps, no uploads, no tracking.
      </p>

      <h2>How it is built</h2>
      <p>
        The whole site is static files generated at build time. Each tool is a
        pure function over text; the interface feeds your paste into that
        function and shows the result. Large inputs are handed to a background
        Web Worker so the page never freezes. There is no database, no
        authentication and no server-side logic — which is exactly why there is
        nothing to leak.
      </p>

      <h2>What is next</h2>
      <p>
        The first release focuses on ten text-cleaning tools, each done
        properly. Next comes a CSV/spreadsheet cluster (dedupe, column
        cleaning) that follows the same rule: files are read in your browser
        with the File API and never uploaded.
      </p>

      <h2>Honest limits</h2>
      <p>
        ScrubKit does not try to replace a spreadsheet or a database. If you
        need joins across columns or millions of rows, use those. For the
        everyday job — paste, clean, copy, leave — a browser tool is faster and
        private by construction.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
